Two players play a prisoner's dilemma every period forever, discounting future payoffs by δ per period. Per-period payoffs: both cooperate 9 each; both defect 7 each; a defector facing a cooperator gets 10 and the cooperator gets 0. Both players use grim trigger: cooperate until a defection is discovered, then defect forever. With perfect monitoring (a defection is seen immediately and punished from the next period), what is the smallest δ that sustains cooperation? Give δ rounded to 4 decimal places. Reply with only the number.